<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Algeciras</h1><p class="st-meta">1035 CE – 1058 CE (approx.) · capital Algeciras</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Hammudid taifa on the Bay of Algeciras, controlling the crossing of the Strait of Gibraltar until Seville seized it in 1058.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a>, the main crossing point to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-morocco">Morocco</a>, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammudid-dynasty">Hammudid</a> possession. Around 1035 a branch of the family under Muhammad ibn al-Qasim made the town and its district a separate principality, while his cousins ruled the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-malaga">Taifa of Málaga</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was small but strategic, controlling the port that linked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a>. Its rulers, like the Málaga line, used the caliphal titles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammudid-dynasty">Hammudids</a> and relied on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> troops. Little more is known about its administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1058 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutadid-of-seville">al-Mutadid</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-seville">Taifa of Seville</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a> and forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasim-ibn-muhammad-of-algeciras">al-Qasim ibn Muhammad</a> to surrender it. Algeciras was later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>' landing place in 1086.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taifa-of-algeciras.jpg" alt="Taifa of Algeciras" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Tyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_Taifa_of_Algeciras.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1035 CE – 1058 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Algeciras</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, al-Qasim ibn Muhammad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Algeciras</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1046&amp;focus=taifa-of-algeciras" aria-label="Taifa of Algeciras on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4543 874 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Algeciras lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4863 1130L4889 1110M4863 1130L4850 1088"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4889 1110h0M4850 1088h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4863 1130h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4863 1130h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Algeciras. <a href="/atlas?year=1046&amp;focus=taifa-of-algeciras">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
